WEBVTT

00:03.050 --> 00:06.420
<i>It's been a month since I learned 
the truth about Substance X.</i>

00:06.420 --> 00:10.780
<i>In that time, I've explored all the way from 
the thirty-first to the fortieth floor.</i>

00:11.460 --> 00:14.660
<i>I started encountering monsters
 I've never seen before,</i>

00:15.230 --> 00:18.720
<i>and I eventually made it
to the fortieth-floor boss battle.</i>

00:20.520 --> 00:22.710
Or, at least, that was the plan...

00:22.710 --> 00:26.170
But something about it gave me 
a bad feeling, you know?

00:26.500 --> 00:30.630
Maybe I can gather more info about 
the undead at the Adventurers' Guild.

00:33.010 --> 00:34.860
Wha—? Oh.

00:41.540 --> 00:46.190
Um, what's wrong, little one? 
Did you want to talk to me?

00:47.400 --> 00:48.500
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:48.500 --> 00:52.670
<i>If I'm spotted with a girl this young, I might
get stuck with another nasty nickname!</i>

00:52.490 --> 00:54.110
<b>Reported!</b>

00:54.770 --> 00:57.490
Welp, why don't we go on inside?

01:02.860 --> 01:05.040
Welcome to the Adventurers' Guild...

01:05.040 --> 01:07.540
St. Weirdo Luciel-sama!

01:08.170 --> 01:09.940
We've been waiting for you!

01:16.510 --> 01:20.760
<b>The Great Cleric</b>

01:17.590 --> 01:20.760
A Salaryman's <b>Path </b>to <b>Surviving Another World</b>

02:45.010 --> 02:48.810
#11 Trouble in St. Shurule

02:45.970 --> 02:48.810
Nanaella-san? Monika-san?

02:48.810 --> 02:49.880
Yes!

02:49.880 --> 02:51.980
What are you two doing here?

02:53.520 --> 02:55.070
All hands! All hands!

02:55.470 --> 02:57.210
St. Weirdo is here!

02:57.210 --> 02:59.850
Bring in the injured from the streets!

02:59.850 --> 03:01.480
Everyone's gonna be saved now!

03:01.480 --> 03:02.660
Huh? Huh?

03:02.660 --> 03:04.580
Hey! Hold on a minute!

03:04.580 --> 03:08.560
I wasn't done talking to them!

03:09.910 --> 03:10.890
Cure!

03:11.470 --> 03:12.580
Recover!

03:12.580 --> 03:14.040
Dispel!

03:16.890 --> 03:18.510
St. Weirdo, over here as well.

03:18.510 --> 03:19.960
Please wait a minute.

03:22.480 --> 03:26.790
That beastfolk child over there 
came to me for help out front.

03:26.790 --> 03:29.060
Would you see what she has to say?

03:29.060 --> 03:30.420
All right.

03:30.830 --> 03:32.090
Thank you.

03:34.980 --> 03:37.500
<i>Monika-san, Nanaella-san...</i>

03:38.660 --> 03:40.760
<i>Why did you come all the way to the capital?</i>

03:43.740 --> 03:45.490
<i>Could it be...?</i>

03:51.150 --> 03:53.330
<i>They're here to tell me
 they're getting married?!</i>

03:53.330 --> 03:57.520
<i>Congratulations?!</i>

03:58.300 --> 04:01.880
<i>No... I'm not gonna cry yet!</i>

04:02.720 --> 04:04.420
I'm better!

04:04.420 --> 04:05.800
It doesn't hurt anymore!

04:05.800 --> 04:07.190
All done.

04:07.190 --> 04:08.430
St. Weirdo?

04:09.010 --> 04:13.810
Would you mind hurrying 
to the slums with this girl?

04:15.770 --> 04:18.270
Um, is it urgent?

04:18.270 --> 04:19.150
Yes.

04:19.150 --> 04:20.340
Luciel-kun.

04:20.780 --> 04:22.850
We'll go with you.

04:22.850 --> 04:23.990
We've got to hurry!

04:24.400 --> 04:26.040
But isn't it dangerous?

04:26.040 --> 04:27.340
The slums, huh?

04:27.340 --> 04:28.460
Master?

04:28.460 --> 04:29.870
I'll go with you.

04:30.700 --> 04:33.080
I'm sure it'll be safer with you there.

04:33.080 --> 04:34.270
We're counting on you!

04:38.810 --> 04:40.750
<i>What a stench.</i>

04:40.750 --> 04:42.950
<i>Is it the smell of death?</i>

04:43.420 --> 04:45.550
<i>There are puddles of blood everywhere.</i>

04:53.850 --> 04:55.600
What happened here?

04:55.600 --> 04:59.280
We heard they're representatives from 
the Independent City-State of Yenice.

04:59.280 --> 05:04.070
When they got close to the border,
they were attacked by a big group of thieves.

05:04.070 --> 05:08.960
Since there's so many of them,
we can't take them all to a clinic.

05:10.280 --> 05:14.100
So she came to the Adventurers' 
Guild to ask for help...

05:18.490 --> 05:19.740
Are you all right?

05:21.590 --> 05:23.880
<i>He's standing up while unconscious?</i>

05:24.330 --> 05:27.890
I-I guess I'll use area high heal.

05:28.850 --> 05:30.150
Luciel-kun!

05:34.060 --> 05:36.190
Ow!

05:37.960 --> 05:40.400
<i>I'm gonna die... I'm gonna die!
I'm gonna die! I'm gonna die!</i>

05:40.400 --> 05:43.580
<i>Again? In a place like this?</i>

05:44.030 --> 05:47.990
<i>No! I'm not the same man I was then.</i>

05:50.800 --> 05:52.950
God, that hurts!

05:53.690 --> 05:55.750
Damn it, I'll heal all of you!

05:55.750 --> 05:57.830
Area high heal!

06:11.450 --> 06:13.090
Luciel-kun, are you okay?

06:13.090 --> 06:14.680
He just stabbed you!

06:14.680 --> 06:17.020
St. Weirdo, I'm sorry.

06:17.020 --> 06:19.080
I never thought anyone would attack you.

06:19.080 --> 06:22.310
He didn't seem threatening. 
Got me before I knew it...

06:22.640 --> 06:25.780
No way we could've seen that coming.

06:25.780 --> 06:30.620
I bet he was instinctively trying 
to protect the other beastfolk.

06:32.100 --> 06:33.700
Purification!

06:33.700 --> 06:35.020
Recover!

06:39.930 --> 06:43.090
That should cover the healing for now.

06:43.810 --> 06:49.170
<i>The guy who stabbed me... 
Is he that girl's father?</i>

06:49.930 --> 06:52.380
<i>Well, I'm glad they're okay.</i>

06:52.380 --> 06:53.470
Excuse me!

06:55.560 --> 06:56.810
We beg you!

06:56.810 --> 06:59.020
Please help the residents here too!

06:59.020 --> 07:01.350
Erm...

07:01.910 --> 07:04.720
<i>What's with the Japanese-style kowtowing?</i>

07:05.400 --> 07:07.280
These are the folks
who live here in the slums.

07:07.890 --> 07:11.240
All I can really do is treat injuries.

07:11.240 --> 07:14.450
Luciel-kun, are you going 
to treat them for free?

07:14.450 --> 07:19.760
Well, there are rules, 
so I can't just do it for free.

07:20.550 --> 07:26.070
<i>I decided to treat the residents, 
but I did it under the pretext of "charity."</i>

07:26.070 --> 07:29.260
<i>Then I purified the area that 
was the source of their plague.</i>

07:29.640 --> 07:33.230
<i>I explained to them that 
I wouldn't always be able to do so</i>

07:33.230 --> 07:35.640
<i>and lectured them on 
the importance of public safety</i>

07:35.640 --> 07:37.680
<i>and the necessity of regular cleaning</i>

07:37.680 --> 07:41.730
<i>to prevent people from 
getting injured and sick.</i>

07:41.730 --> 07:45.980
St. Weirdo! St. Weirdo!
St. Weirdo! St. Weirdo!

07:45.980 --> 07:50.870
St. Weirdo! St. Weirdo!
St. Weirdo! St. Weirdo!

07:46.830 --> 07:50.080
<i>But who the heck told them 
to call me "St. Weirdo"?</i>

07:51.200 --> 07:54.160
<b>Holy Capital of Shurule, City Center</b>

07:56.570 --> 08:01.290
Sorry to get you caught up in that after 
you came all the way to the capital.

08:01.290 --> 08:02.920
It's okay.

08:02.920 --> 08:06.060
But I wish you would think 
a little more about yourself.

08:06.480 --> 08:10.510
I was really shaken when 
you got stabbed like that.

08:11.670 --> 08:15.510
<i>Man, it feels great to have someone
care about me! I'm so happy!</i>

08:15.510 --> 08:19.520
<i>This might give me the boost I need 
to fight the boss on the fortieth level.</i>

08:15.510 --> 08:22.140
<b>Touched...</b>

08:19.520 --> 08:22.560
<i>Must be a surprise from Monster Luck-sensei.</i>

08:22.560 --> 08:24.860
Sure has been a while, boy!

08:25.350 --> 08:27.020
Luciel-kun?

08:27.020 --> 08:28.900
Ah! S-Sorry!

08:28.900 --> 08:32.450
By the way, what brings you two to the capital?

08:32.450 --> 08:35.570
I bet the guild's got it rough
without its receptionists.

08:35.570 --> 08:40.200
I'm sure you're right, especially now
that two of them are getting married.

08:40.200 --> 08:41.040
Right.

08:41.040 --> 08:42.750
<i>M-Married...</i>

08:42.750 --> 08:47.250
So we decided to visit the capital 
before things get really busy.

08:47.250 --> 08:51.020
U-Um... So who exactly is getting married?

08:51.020 --> 08:52.090
Huh?

08:52.650 --> 08:54.840
It's Melina-san and Mernell-san.

08:54.840 --> 08:55.970
Huh?

08:55.970 --> 08:59.030
But we told you that in our letters. 
Right, Nana-chan?

08:59.030 --> 09:00.010
Yeah.

09:01.060 --> 09:02.910
You've both been sending me letters?

09:02.910 --> 09:04.770
W-Well, yes.

09:04.770 --> 09:07.910
I kept writing to you
but never got a response,

09:07.910 --> 09:11.900
so I thought maybe you didn't want 
them and I should stop writing.

09:11.900 --> 09:12.810
Huh?

09:12.810 --> 09:15.360
We haven't received a single 
letter from you, though!

09:17.450 --> 09:20.070
Does that mean Master Brod
didn't get any either?

09:20.070 --> 09:24.130
I think he did. He seemed 
really happy about it.

09:24.130 --> 09:28.040
But that was the only one
that came, wasn't it?

09:29.730 --> 09:31.380
Ah, sorry, sorry.

09:31.720 --> 09:34.720
I always party after I'm done with work.

09:34.720 --> 09:38.550
I've still got your letters. I just 
forgot to have them sent, darn it.

09:38.550 --> 09:43.020
<i>What do you mean you "forgot," darn it?!</i>

09:43.020 --> 09:44.780
By the way, St. Weirdo...

09:44.780 --> 09:46.680
Oh, Elitz-dono.

09:47.230 --> 09:50.480
Which one of these ladies is your girlfriend?

09:49.940 --> 09:53.150
Girlfriend

09:52.320 --> 09:53.150
Huh?!

09:53.150 --> 09:55.340
Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-What are you talking about?

09:55.340 --> 09:59.360
Those are the renowned receptionist babes
 from Merratoni, right?

09:59.360 --> 10:02.980
They've been with him the whole time 
he was healing. Even in the slums!

10:02.980 --> 10:05.830
Seriously?! You think
he's dating both of them?

10:05.830 --> 10:08.680
How does a guy with a nickname 
like <i>that</i> get so lucky?

10:08.680 --> 10:10.550
<i>What's that supposed to mean?!</i>

10:10.550 --> 10:13.300
<i>I mean, I never ask to be called that!</i>

10:14.130 --> 10:18.230
These ladies are the reason
I was able to become a healer.

10:18.230 --> 10:19.720
They're very dear to me.

10:20.800 --> 10:25.320
Thanks to their support, I was able 
to keep all that Substance X down

10:25.320 --> 10:29.520
and survive Master Brod's training, 
and that's no exaggeration.

10:29.520 --> 10:31.230
B-Brod?!

10:31.230 --> 10:34.200
B-Brod? You mean the Whirlwind?

10:36.070 --> 10:39.220
Now then, how long do you plan on staying?

10:39.220 --> 10:41.070
We'll be here three nights.

10:41.070 --> 10:47.040
I-In that case, I'd like to spend as much 
time with you as possible!

10:47.040 --> 10:48.310
Sure!

10:49.910 --> 10:51.500
In that case...

10:52.230 --> 10:52.970
Huh?

10:53.750 --> 10:54.580
Huh?

10:55.380 --> 10:57.960
We just heard from the receptionist here...

10:58.270 --> 11:00.680
There are some injured 
folks in the training hall.

11:00.680 --> 11:01.990
So, time for work!

11:02.390 --> 11:06.600
B-But you traveled all this way...
Is this really what you want to do?

11:06.600 --> 11:07.630
Of course!

11:07.630 --> 11:09.350
Because we'll be with you!

11:13.430 --> 11:14.950
Ah, to be young...

11:15.650 --> 11:17.540
<i>One thing led to the next,</i>

11:17.540 --> 11:21.460
<i>and we didn't really do anything 
special during their visit.</i>

11:21.460 --> 11:23.560
<i>We just treated adventurers.</i>

11:23.560 --> 11:29.250
<i>As an apology for the letters, the master 
held a huge party for everyone.</i>

11:29.250 --> 11:34.070
<i>And before we knew it, it was time 
for them to leave the capital.</i>

11:35.230 --> 11:38.710
I'm so happy that you came to visit!

11:38.710 --> 11:42.630
And we're really happy we 
got to see you doing so well.

11:42.630 --> 11:43.450
Yeah.

11:45.420 --> 11:48.870
Next time, I'll try to come visit you instead.

11:49.500 --> 11:51.260
I can't wait!

11:53.400 --> 11:55.020
We synced!

11:57.390 --> 12:00.610
<i>I feel like their visit gave me energy 
to keep fighting through the labyrinth.</i>

12:00.980 --> 12:03.570
<i>The energy to do my absolute best.</i>

12:04.120 --> 12:06.940
<i>I look forward to the day we can meet again.</i>

12:15.440 --> 12:17.880
Japanese-style kowtowing

12:17.880 --> 12:21.630
Um, would you please stand up now?

12:21.630 --> 12:24.130
The stab wound has already healed completely.

12:24.130 --> 12:28.860
I can't possibly! You're such 
an esteemed, high-ranking healer!

12:28.860 --> 12:31.780
There's absolutely no excuse 
for me injuring you!

12:31.780 --> 12:34.350
I could give my life 
and it still wouldn't be enough!

12:34.350 --> 12:36.990
No, that really isn't necessary!

12:36.990 --> 12:41.420
Thankfully, we were able to save your life,
so don't throw it away.

12:42.650 --> 12:47.120
<b>Touched</b>

12:43.810 --> 12:45.420
St. Weirdo!

12:47.240 --> 12:48.900
Oh, is that right?

12:48.900 --> 12:52.750
You came all this way because you want 
to found a Healers' Guild in Yenice?

12:52.750 --> 12:57.630
Thanks to you, our meeting 
with the pope went very well.

12:57.630 --> 13:02.050
We were only able to do this 
because you saved our lives.

13:02.050 --> 13:04.480
We really cannot thank you enough!

13:04.480 --> 13:07.250
No, not at all! It was truly nothing.

13:07.250 --> 13:08.290
No, hardly!

13:08.290 --> 13:09.320
No, truly! I insist!

13:09.320 --> 13:10.350
No, it was really and truly...

13:11.720 --> 13:12.720
Ah!

13:13.620 --> 13:15.910
Oh, it's you.

13:15.910 --> 13:17.790
H-Hey, Sheila!

13:17.790 --> 13:20.440
St. Weirdo, I apologize 
for my daughter's behavior.

13:20.440 --> 13:23.130
No need to worry. It's perfectly fine.

13:24.750 --> 13:27.240
<i>I wonder if this girl...</i>

13:27.240 --> 13:32.960
Long ago, my daughter's vocal cords 
were damaged in an accident.

13:32.960 --> 13:34.430
Oh, I see.

13:36.840 --> 13:41.590
Sheila-chan, you're a hero 
for saving all these people.

13:46.970 --> 13:50.800
Never let fate hold you back. 
Keep doing your best!

13:56.450 --> 13:59.230
St. Weirdo, did you say something?

14:01.300 --> 14:03.390
It was just a little blessing.

14:04.380 --> 14:06.020
<i>Extra heal.</i>

14:06.700 --> 14:10.220
<i>I haven't mastered it yet, 
so it might have no effect,</i>

14:10.600 --> 14:15.160
<i>but I hope it helps Sheila-chan regain 
at least a little of her voice.</i>

14:21.010 --> 14:25.550
I see. So you've made it all the way 
to the main chamber of the fortieth floor.

14:23.000 --> 14:25.550
<b>Valkyrie Paladin Regiment Training Grounds</b>

14:25.550 --> 14:29.210
But when I think about the tough 
enemy waiting there for me,

14:29.210 --> 14:32.110
I'm worried I might not 
be ready to fight him yet.

14:32.800 --> 14:34.210
You're a coward.

14:34.890 --> 14:37.430
Though I don't think that's 
necessarily a bad thing.

14:38.390 --> 14:41.460
When exploring the labyrinth, 
you put your life on the line.

14:41.460 --> 14:43.830
If you're feeling unsure, 
why don't we spar some more?

14:43.830 --> 14:45.820
What? You mean it?

14:45.820 --> 14:49.610
It's almost been a year since you 
came to headquarters, Luciel-kun.

14:50.450 --> 14:53.320
I want to see how much 
you've improved since then.

14:56.340 --> 14:57.420
All right.

15:02.140 --> 15:04.040
Thanks for doing this with me!

15:09.090 --> 15:13.550
<i>Even using my physical enhancement skill,
it takes everything I have to defend.</i>

15:13.550 --> 15:15.970
<i>Lumina-san really is amazing.</i>

15:15.970 --> 15:18.930
<i>So I'm gonna have to try something unorthodox</i>

15:18.930 --> 15:19.640
<i>if I want to win!</i>

15:24.010 --> 15:24.880
Uh...

15:27.850 --> 15:30.360
<i>I bet she's gonna be mad about that.</i>

15:32.820 --> 15:35.600
You managed to surprise me, Luciel-kun.

15:36.120 --> 15:39.000
I had no idea you'd become this strong.

15:42.330 --> 15:45.770
Why don't you try attacking me 
this time, Luciel-kun?

15:45.770 --> 15:46.910
Here I come!

15:52.040 --> 15:55.600
In less than a year, you've 
already gotten lots better.

15:57.060 --> 16:01.890
But you probably still shouldn't try 
to fight super strong opponents yet.

16:02.280 --> 16:07.470
Thanks for the advice. I have
a better idea of how to proceed now.

16:07.470 --> 16:10.360
Keep your eyes on the prize 
and do your best, 'kay?

16:12.320 --> 16:16.100
Can I ask why you've gotten
so much more casual with me, Lumina-san?

16:19.050 --> 16:23.590
Well, that's... actually 
the way I normally talk.

16:23.590 --> 16:27.690
I make an effort to sound tougher, 
but sometimes I let my guard down.

16:28.590 --> 16:33.560
I think the friendly tone really suits you.

16:37.010 --> 16:38.840
I'll remember that.

16:38.840 --> 16:43.730
But the female paladins 
I respect also talk tough like this.

16:43.730 --> 16:44.920
Is that right?

16:44.920 --> 16:50.330
Well, if you ever want to be casual,
I'm always happy to chat.

16:52.080 --> 16:54.150
When the time is right.

16:55.110 --> 16:59.670
<i>The next day, with Lumina-san leading them,</i>

16:59.670 --> 17:02.080
<i>the Valkyrie paladin regiment 
set out for the border.</i>

17:02.830 --> 17:05.580
<b>Six Months Later</b>

17:04.270 --> 17:08.590
I see. You've finally decided to go 
to the fortieth-floor main chamber.

17:08.590 --> 17:09.380
Yes.

17:09.380 --> 17:13.180
I've spent enough time training
and finally made up my mind.

17:13.180 --> 17:17.300
Lumina asked me to give you 
this letter when the time came.

17:18.660 --> 17:20.070
Lumina-san did?

17:21.010 --> 17:24.560
<b>Fortieth Level</b>

17:27.290 --> 17:29.960
<i>In the level forty main chamber, 
you will most likely find</i>

17:29.960 --> 17:34.300
<i>a man who used his exceptional spearmanship
to climb the ranks and become head templar,</i>

17:34.300 --> 17:38.310
<i>and a knight who used his powerful
recovery magic and long sword technique</i>

17:38.310 --> 17:41.330
<i>to fight his way to become 
captain of the paladins.</i>

17:47.900 --> 17:51.220
<i>I guess both powerful foes 
merged into one undead monster</i>

17:51.220 --> 17:54.070
<i>that dual wields a sword 
</i>and<i> a spear. That's gotta be it.</i>

17:54.440 --> 17:58.560
<i>That's so unfair! That's the fighting 
style </i>I<i> wanted to use!</i>

17:58.560 --> 18:00.080
Purification!

18:03.790 --> 18:05.310
<i>No effect?</i>

18:05.310 --> 18:07.100
<i>Then what about physical attacks?</i>

18:09.630 --> 18:10.940
<i>Did that work?</i>

18:13.210 --> 18:15.110
<i>Physical attacks may be effective,</i>

18:15.110 --> 18:17.650
<i>but I have no way to tell 
how much damage they deal.</i>

18:18.150 --> 18:21.280
<i>More importantly, fighting like this 
is going to wear me out.</i>

18:41.870 --> 18:44.470
<i>That saved me! But...</i>

18:45.360 --> 18:48.110
<i>Really, what is up with Substance X?</i>

18:48.940 --> 18:52.650
<b>Lost after aggravating the boss with extra heal!</b>

18:48.940 --> 18:52.650
<i>And so I tried all sorts of attacks.</i>

18:52.650 --> 18:56.360
<b>Lost an entire arm, shield and all.</b>

18:52.980 --> 18:57.300
<i>When he got me, I'd retreat to the 
safe zone I cordoned off with Substance X.</i>

18:56.360 --> 19:00.070
<b>Seriously? Sleeping during a boss battle?</b>

18:57.300 --> 18:59.370
<i>I kept repeating that over and over.</i>

19:01.360 --> 19:03.280
<b>One Week Later</b>

19:05.890 --> 19:08.910
<i>I wonder how long it's been 
since I started fighting him.</i>

19:10.120 --> 19:14.560
<i>I'm gonna run out of food soon.
I really don't want to starve to death!</i>

19:14.560 --> 19:16.120
<i>But at this rate...</i>

19:16.800 --> 19:19.170
<b>Oh, dear Luciel...</b>

19:19.170 --> 19:21.630
<b>What a shame that you died.</b>

19:21.630 --> 19:25.550
<i>No, no, no, no, no!
This isn't some kind of video game!</i>

19:25.560 --> 19:30.620
<i>I'd already started to suspect it,
but this isn't a fake labyrinth after all.</i>

19:30.620 --> 19:32.450
<i>It's actually the real deal.</i>

19:32.440 --> 19:37.400
<b>Name: Luciel</b>

19:32.440 --> 19:37.400
<b>Job: Healer VIII</b>

19:32.440 --> 19:37.400
<b>Age: 18</b>

19:32.440 --> 19:37.400
<b>Level: 1</b>

19:32.820 --> 19:35.680
<i>I still don't know why my level won't go up,</i>

19:35.680 --> 19:40.120
<i>but it finally dawned on me
after losing limbs and nearly dying...</i>

19:41.580 --> 19:43.690
<i>If I get killed, it's really game over.</i>

19:43.690 --> 19:45.660
<i>There's no reset or new game.</i>

19:46.630 --> 19:49.120
<i>If I don't win, I'm done for good.</i>

19:53.420 --> 19:57.340
<i>I've got this. I've fought him 
long enough to learn his attack patterns.</i>

19:57.340 --> 19:59.870
<i>And over the last half a year,</i>

19:59.870 --> 20:02.680
<i>I've visualized how to win
against a dual-wielding opponent</i>

20:02.680 --> 20:05.510
<i>over and over again in my head.</i>

20:06.050 --> 20:07.120
<i>Now's my chance!</i>

20:08.020 --> 20:10.560
<i>I first need to stop his continuous attacks,</i>

20:10.560 --> 20:12.020
<i>and once I do...</i>

20:13.690 --> 20:16.860
<i>he's not big on defense,
so he'll be wide open!</i>

20:18.820 --> 20:23.490
No matter how high your status gets, if your 
head is chopped off your body, you're dead.

20:24.840 --> 20:28.740
<i>I'm not sure if that's true for the 
undead, but I'll trust my master.</i>

20:28.740 --> 20:32.500
<i>There are people I want to see again.</i>

20:32.900 --> 20:35.130
<i>They're giving me the will to survive!</i>

20:37.140 --> 20:38.480
<i>Because at this point,</i>

20:40.220 --> 20:43.070
<i>I've given up on giving up!</i>

20:48.830 --> 20:50.940
I... I did it!

20:56.160 --> 20:58.910
Cattleya-san is probably worried about me.

20:58.910 --> 21:01.260
I should go back for now.

21:02.360 --> 21:06.260
Man, that really was a long uphill battle.

21:12.540 --> 21:17.490
Oh, silly me. I have to push it, not pull!

21:17.490 --> 21:20.140
I was fighting for so long, 
I must've forgotten.

21:30.940 --> 21:32.990
It still won't open...

21:45.790 --> 21:47.030
This really reeks!

21:47.030 --> 21:50.500
But it's top-tier monster repellent,
so I strapped it to myself!

21:50.500 --> 21:54.660
I'll call it the Substance X charge!

21:54.660 --> 21:59.470
<i>After I beat the floor forty boss, 
since I couldn't return to the surface,</i>

21:59.470 --> 22:02.250
<i>I had no choice but to advance 
down to the fiftieth level.</i>

22:02.610 --> 22:06.190
<i>I just walked straight ahead,
stumbling across treasure chests as I went,</i>

22:06.190 --> 22:09.210
<i>and very easily found 
the staircases to the next levels.</i>

22:09.210 --> 22:14.320
<i>It went so smoothly that it was like 
Monster Luck-sensei was showing me the way.</i>

22:14.320 --> 22:16.350
Fight on, boy!

22:16.350 --> 22:20.540
<i>And at last, I found myself
at the fiftieth-floor boss.</i>

23:55.510 --> 23:57.390
Boy, I've sure been through a lot!

23:56.450 --> 23:57.790
<b>Sanctuary Circle</b>

23:57.390 --> 24:00.960
Master Brod put me through the wringer, 
I had to drink tons of Substance X,

24:00.960 --> 24:02.040
<b>St. Weirdo</b>

24:00.960 --> 24:03.740
and I almost died so many times in 
the labyrinth. Wait, what?

24:03.740 --> 24:07.010
Next time: "S-Rank Healer and 
Exorcist Luciel's Declaration"!

24:04.670 --> 24:09.960
#12 S-Rank Healer and Exorcist Luciel's Declaration

24:07.010 --> 24:09.960
Hold it! I'm not a "great" anything yet!
